<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 9.997 percent from 9.999 percent at the previous auction on January 27.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Aug 5, 1997 (July 19, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.997 percent (9.999)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 702.375 million (903.675 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 902.375 million (1,160.275 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.380-10.101 percent (8.987-10.061)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.380-10.300 percent (8.987-10.300)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 124 (124)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 126 (151)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
